[40.038442, "o", "I have everything needed. Here is the complete preflight report.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🔴 Preflight Verdict: BLOCK\r\n\r\n> **This upgrade must NOT proceed.**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 1. Verdict\r\n\r\n```\r\nBLOCK\r\n```\r\n\r\nExit code: `2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 2. Fingerprint\r\n\r\n```\r\n80483bd4091749dd  (first 20 chars of full: 80483bd4091749dd4b4f9b7642d832e761bbe24d30decc2c57343027e3453142)\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 3. Security Findings\r\n\r\nBoth findings are **new** (not pre-existing in the baseline).\r\n\r\n| # | Rule ID | Severity | Kind / Name | json_path | Message | Pre-existing? |\r\n|---|---------|----------|-------------|-----------|---------|---------------|\r\n| 1 | **RBAC-001** | 🔴 CRITICAL | `ClusterRole/demo-app-reader` | `$.rules[0].resources` | Wildcard `*` in resources grants access to **all resource types** | ❌ No |\r\n| 2 | **RBAC-002** | 🔴 CRITICAL | `ClusterRole/demo-app-reader` | `$.rules[0].verbs` | Wildcard `*` in verbs grants **all operations** | ❌ No |\r\n\r\nBoth findings carry `verdict_contribution: BLOCK` and were evaluated by **conftest**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 4. Diff Summary\r\n\r\n| Added | Modified | Removed |\r\n|-------|----------|---------|\r\n| 0 | **1** | 0 |\r\n\r\nThe single modified resource is `ClusterRole/demo-app-reader`. The candidate's `$.rules` changed from:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# baseline (safe)\r\n- apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n  resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n  verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nto:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# candidate (blocked)\r\n- apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n  resources: [\"*\"]\r\n  verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 5. No Deployment Occurred\r\n\r\n```\r\nrun_metadata.no_deployment_occurred: true  ✅\r\noperation.no_deployment_occurred:    true  ✅\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis was a fully offline, read-only evaluation. No cluster credentials were used.\r\n\r\nEvidence completeness: **COMPLETE** (no limitations). Rendering stability confirmed: **true**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🔧 Remediation — Smallest Concrete Fix\r\n\r\nThe candidate chart has a single template file: `examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml`\r\n\r\n**Current (broken):**\r\n```yaml\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n    resources: [\"*\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Fix — replace wildcards with the least-privilege explicit lists your application actually needs:**\r\n```yaml\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is the minimum change that eliminates both RBAC-001 and RBAC-002:\r\n- Replace `apiGroups: [\"*\"]` → `[\"\"]` (core API group only, or list specific groups needed)\r\n- Replace `resources: [\"*\"]` → an explicit allowlist (e.g. `[\"pods\", \"services\"]`)\r\n- Replace `verbs: [\"*\"]` → an explicit allowlist (e.g. `[\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]`)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## ✅ Which Example Chart Would Pass Instead — and Why\r\n\r\n**`examples/safe-upgrade`** would pass. Its candidate chart (`examples/safe-upgrade/candidate/templates/deployment.yaml`) makes only a single, benign change:\r\n\r\n> `image: nginx:1.24.0` → `image: nginx:1.25.0`\r\n\r\nThis triggers **zero RBAC or workload security findings** because:\r\n- No RBAC resources are modified\r\n- No privileged containers, hostNetwork/hostPID/hostIPC, or hostPath mounts are introduced\r\n- The diff is a 1-field container image bump — minimal blast radius\r\n- All policy rules (RBAC-001/002, WORK-001 through WORK-006) remain unchallenged\r\n\r\nThe `rbac-escalation` candidate, by contrast, introduced **cluster-wide wildcard permissions** — a textbook privilege escalation — which the policy correctly blocks.\r\n"]
